  "glossary": [
    {
      "term": "idempotency key",
      "full": "Identifier shared by retries of one operation",
      "note": "Use only when the provider supports saving and returning a prior outcome."
    }
  ],
  "beats": [
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Tess draws a payment path: client, service, storage. Then adds retry loops everywhere.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "seq.diagram",
          "id": "retry",
          "actors": [
            "Client",
            "Service",
            "Storage"
          ],
          "messages": [
            {
              "from": "Client",
              "to": "Service",
              "label": "payment request"
            },
            {
              "from": "Service",
              "to": "Storage",
              "label": "write"
            }
          ],
          "at": "start"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "illustrative topology; no measured traffic",
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "rookie",
      "text": "Three attempts per layer, including the first try. Every component gets another chance. What could go wrong?",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "Tess adds retry loops everywhere",
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "senior",
      "text": "Three layers with three tries each can yield twenty-seven downstream tries for one request.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "tree",
          "id": "attempts",
          "nodes": [
            {
              "id": "request",
              "label": "1 logical request"
            },
            {
              "id": "client",
              "label": "3 client tries",
              "parent": "request"
            },
            {
              "id": "service",
              "label": "3 per call",
              "parent": "client"
            },
            {
              "id": "storage",
              "label": "3 per call",
              "parent": "service"
            }
          ],
          "path": [
            "request",
            "client",
            "service",
            "storage"
          ],
          "at": "start"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "illustrative arithmetic: 3 × 3 × 3",
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "rookie",
      "text": "I will add exponential backoff. Surely waiting longer stops everybody colliding again?",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "Tess types a fixed backoff",
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "senior",
      "text": "Backoff alone can synchronize clients. Add jitter by choosing a random delay inside a capped exponential window.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "code.editor",
          "id": "policy",
          "title": "Illustrative retry policy",
          "lines": [
            "window = min(cap, base * 2**attempt)",
            "delay = random(0, window)"
          ],
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "rookie",
      "text": "Then one layer owns retries. But how do I stop it trying all night?",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "Tess adds deadline check",
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "senior",
      "text": "Bound attempts and the overall deadline. A retry budget also limits recovery traffic across requests.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "code.editor",
          "id": "bounds",
          "title": "Bound the work",
          "lines": [
            "if attempts >= limit: stop",
            "if budget is empty: stop",
            "if deadline_left <= delay: stop"
          ],
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "rookie",
      "text": "The payment timed out. I can send a new payment now, because the first failed.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "payment timed out",
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "senior",
      "text": "The write may have committed before its reply was lost. Timeout means unknown, not failed.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "seq.diagram",
          "id": "outcome",
          "actors": [
            "Service",
            "Provider"
          ],
          "messages": [
            {
              "from": "Service",
              "to": "Provider",
              "label": "payment accepted"
            },
            {
              "from": "Provider",
              "to": "Service",
              "label": "reply lost",
              "reply": true
            }
          ],
          "at": "start"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "request outcome unknown",
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "rookie",
      "text": "Reuse one idempotency key for the same operation, under the provider’s deduplication contract.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "code.editor",
          "id": "dedupe",
          "title": "Provider-supported idempotency",
          "lines": [
            "same key → same logical operation",
            "provider returns saved outcome",
            "no duplicate side effect"
          ],
          "at": "start"
        },
        {
          "do": "define",
          "term": "idempotency key",
          "at": "start"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "same key → same logical operation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "senior",
      "text": "Exactly. That contract needs to cover your retry window. Count application attempts separately from transport retransmissions.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "request ID → application attempt count",
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "rookie",
      "text": "I am deleting the extra retry loops. One owner, bounded work, jitter, and the same payment key.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "Tess edits the design",
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sources": [
    "https://aws.amazon.com/builders-library/timeouts-retries-and-backoff-with-jitter/"
  ],
  "key_points": [
    "Retries at multiple layers multiply downstream attempts during a slow dependency.",
    "Use a single retry owner, capped exponential backoff with jitter, an attempt limit, and an overall deadline or budget.",
    "A timeout leaves the outcome unknown; use a stored idempotency result before retrying side effects."
  ],
